{
	"Name": "Search - LLM - Semantic - Prompt Injection and Jailbreak Attempts [table]",
	"Description": "Finds prompts whose *meaning* is an attempt to override the model's instructions or extract its system prompt, regardless of the exact wording used. Keyword rules miss paraphrases; this does not.\n\nRequires embeddings on the entries (vector preprocessor on the LLM listener) and an embedding model configured in the webserver's [AI] section. Without both, this query returns nothing. Tune sensitivity with the LLM_SEMANTIC_THRESHOLD config macro rather than editing the query.\n\n`embeddings` is an intrinsic enumerated value, so it is declared on the intrinsic extraction module alongside everything else the query needs; the semantic module cannot see it otherwise.",
	"GUID": "7875ca64-6a13-5ef1-a3a2-aa733056be6b",
